# Create endpoint: POST http://127.0.0.1:5001/api/v1/orders (no /create suffix).
# Prerequisites: login -> select or create brand/category/product/customer in the other files.
# IDs and sessions are shared automatically through REST_CLIENT/.env.
# IMPORTANT: completion and cancellation below are ALTERNATIVE workflows, not one sequence.
# A Rejected (3) or Completed (4) order is final. Do not reuse it for another status test.
# ORDER_ID is refreshed after each successful create; create a NEW order for each workflow.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5001/api/v1/orders
@customerId = {{$dotenv CUSTOMER_ID}}
@productId = {{$dotenv PRODUCT_ID}}
@variantId = {{$dotenv VARIANT_ID}}
@userId = {{$dotenv USER_ID}}
@orderId = {{$dotenv ORDER_ID}}

### Route check only (expected 400 validation error; does NOT create an order)
# @name checkOrderEndpoint
POST http://127.0.0.1:5001/api/v1/orders
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Create an order for the selected variant (Pending = 1)
# @name createOrder
POST http://127.0.0.1:5001/api/v1/orders
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "orderNote": "REST Client test order",
  "street": "123 Test Street",
  "city": "Da Nang",
  "state": "Da Nang",
  "paymentType": 1,
  "orderItems": [
    { "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### List orders
GET {{baseUrl}}?page=1&limit=10
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Filter pending orders for the customer
GET {{baseUrl}}?page=1&limit=10&orderStatus=1&customerId={{customerId}}
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Get order details
# @name inspectOrderStatus
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### FLOW A - Step 1: Pending -> Processing (2). Check current orderStatus is 1 first.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}/status
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderStatus": 2, "userId": "{{userId}}" }

### Reassign an open order (admin only; status is preserved)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}/assignee
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{$dotenv STAFF_USER_ID}}" }

### FLOW A - Step 2: Processing -> Completed (4). STOP this workflow here.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}/status
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderStatus": 4 }

### FLOW B - Alternative: create a NEW order and select its ID, then Pending/Processing -> Rejected (3)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}/status
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderStatus": 3 }

### FLOW B - After rejection only: delete the rejected test order
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}

### Invalid transition: run immediately after creating a fresh Pending order (expected 409)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}/status
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderStatus": 4 }

### Insufficient variant stock (expected 409)
POST http://127.0.0.1:5001/api/v1/orders
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "street": "123 Test Street",
  "city": "Da Nang",
  "state": "Da Nang",
  "paymentType": 1,
  "orderItems": [
    { "productId": "{{productId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 999999 }
  ]
}

### Invalid product ID (expected 400)
POST http://127.0.0.1:5001/api/v1/orders
x-rest-client-auth: primary
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv ACCESS_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "street": "123 Test Street",
  "city": "Da Nang",
  "state": "Da Nang",
  "paymentType": 1,
  "orderItems": [{ "productId": "invalid-id", "quantity": 1 }]
}

### Missing authentication (expected 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}

### Staff cannot delete orders - send staffLogin in auth.http first (expected 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{orderId}}
x-rest-client-auth: staff
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv STAFF_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
